(task (id "38603468") (title "Native: 32-bit values with a tag bit in wasm built through C (halve block size)") (state "todo") (priority 3) (assignee "") (labels "native" "perf" "wasm") (parent "") (details "D90 widens values to 64 bits so blocks and integers can be told apart in wasm32; this doubles block size and makes list sorts 1.1-1.8x slower than the never-freeing --wasm back end (docs/spec/NATIVE.md#wasm-through-c). A low tag bit on Int (or on pointers) keeps 32-bit words but changes every arithmetic op in both back ends.") (links) (comments))
